rachel: Starting a tiny docs PR to tidy up function/tool calling + structured output guidance. main items: short migration path from regex -> json_schema, a guardrails section (common pitfalls), tiny py/ts snippets, and a note about streaming edge cases. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/1770 :sparkles:
ty: nice. can you add an explicit example of a schema that fails gracefully (i.e., returns errors) and how to fallback to a text parser? support tickets often show customers unsure what to do when validation fails
emma: also flag the SDK naming difference early: python uses structured_output (snake_case) and JS/TS uses structuredOutput (camelCase). small copy mistake in previous docs mixed them and caused confusion
rachel: will do. drafting micro-snippets here for quick review:
```python
# python: call tool with JSON Schema + simple fallback
from redwood import RedwoodClient
c = RedwoodClient()
resp = c.call_tool(
    name="extract_totals",
    input={"text": "Invoice..."},
    structured_output={
        "type": "json_schema",
        "schema": {"type":"object","properties":{"total":{"type":"number"}},"required":["total"]}
    }
)
if getattr(resp, 'errors', None):
    # fallback: try best-effort text parse or return structured error
    fallback = fallback_text_parser(resp.raw_text)
    log.warn("schema validation failed, used fallback", resp.errors)
else:
    use_validated(resp.output)
```
```ts
// typescript: similar pattern (camelCase keys)
import { RedClient } from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new RedClient();
const res = await client.callTool({
  name: 'extract_totals',
  input: { text: 'Invoice...' },
  structuredOutput: {
    type: 'json_schema',
    schema: { type: 'object', properties: { total: { type: 'number' } }, required: ['total'] }
  }
});
if (res.errors && res.errors.length) {
  // simple fallback
  const fallback = fallbackTextParser(res.rawText);
  console.warn('validation failed, used fallback', res.errors);
} else {
  handleValidated(res.output);
}
```
rachel: adding a short "guardrails" bullet list: - prefer required fields minimally to avoid frequent false negatives - prefer numeric types over strings for amounts - avoid overly permissive `additionalProperties` unless intentional - test in validation:warn mode for a day before enforcing
ty: good. add a streaming caveat: when streaming=true partial JSON is possible; recommend buffer_full_response or stream=false for critical checks. link runtime issue: https://github.com/redwood-inference/runtime/issues/432
emma: two small doc fixes: replace /docs/structured-output/#jsonschema -> /docs/structured-output/#json-schema and update internal anchor for tool calling to /docs/tool-calling/ so old links stop 404ing. include these in PR notes so changelog picks them up
rachel: also adding a short migration checklist for teams moving off regex: 1) catalog prompts using regex extraction 2) write minimal schema with required keys 3) run in warn mode and collect metrics 4) enable enforce and backport docs for pinned branches if needed
ty: can you include a tiny example showing a regex fallback snippet? some customers prefer a code example rather than prose
rachel: adding one-line fallback sample in the PR as text; will push in ~10m. tagging @devex for visibility :bell:
